  "evidence": "Original N/E/U show a sustained ~5 mm N, ~-22 mm E, ~-2.5 mm U offset beginning near day 599 and returning near day 638–639, with interior points (e.g., days 605–635) consistently offset and smooth—consistent with a genuine temporary platform. P1 (598–601) and P2 (599) are too short and likely capture only onset; P3 (600–638) aligns with the sustained offset but ends one day before the clear return at 639; P4 (638) is the isolated return spike; P5 (640–643) is a later independent step. The return is best observed at day 639 in E/N (sharp reversal from -22 to ~-1), and U recovers gradually. Thus, the genuine temporary platform spans ~599–639, supported by persistent interior offset and coherent return across axes. No other candidate pair forms a complete, nonoverlapping genuine platform.",
  "pair_ids": ["P3", "P4"]
}
